          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-morphisms"} 1-morphisms
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            form an
            %strong adjunction
            if they are
            %strong dual
            to each other (
            %a{:href => "#Lambek82"}> Lambek (1982)
            , cf.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#CategoryTheoryIsTheoryOfDuality"} here
          %p There are two archetypical classes of examples:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}A
                denotes the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton"} one-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                2-category whose single
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-category"} hom-category
                is
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                (the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
                of
                = succeed ")," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}A
                coincides precisely with the notion of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dualizable+object"} dual objects
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+vector+spaces"} dual vector spaces
                in the case that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo =
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A =
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinDimVect"} FinDimVect
            %li
              %p
                Adjunctions in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
                are
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    Notice that essentially everything that makes
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
                    nontrivial and interesting, beyond
                    = succeed "-theory," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+constructions"} universal constructions
                    such as
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limits and colimits
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extensions"} Kan extensions
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coend"} co
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ends"} ends
                    are examples of adjunctions in
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
                %li
                  %p
                    Similarly, for
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi V
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                    any
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmos+for+enrichment"} cosmos for enrichment
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/VCat"} VCat
                    of
                    = succeed "-" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi V
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+categories"} enriched categories
                    are equivalently
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+adjoint+functors"} enriched adjoint functors
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi V
                          %mo =
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V =
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+values"} truth values
                    this subsumes classical concepts such as that of
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+connections"} Galois connections
                %li
                  %p
                    Remarkably, even adjunctions in the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+2-category"} homotopy 2-category
                    of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"}
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn ∞
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                      \-categories
                    are equivalent to
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+%28infinity%2C1%29-functors"}
                        adjoint
                        = succeed "-functors" do
                          %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                            %semantics
                              %mrow
                                %mn ∞
                              %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a{:href => "#AdjointInfinityOneFunctors"} below
              %p
                These classes of examples make adjunctions a key notion in
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+category+theory"} formal category theory
          %p
            Finally, the notion of
            %em adjunction
            may usefully be thought of as a generalization of the notion of
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+a+2-category"} equivalence in a 2-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-morphism"} 1-morphism
            need not be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invertible+morphism"} invertible
            (even up to
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-isomorphism"} 2-isomorphism
            %em a left inverse from below
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %em a right inverse from above
          %p
            If an adjoint 1-morphisms happens to be a genuine
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+a+2-category"} equivalence in a 2-category
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+equivalence"} adjoint equivalence
