          %h2#references References
          %p
            Adjunctions in 2-categories were introduced (together with the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-categories"} strict 2-categories
            itself) in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Marie+Maranda"}> Jean-Marie Maranda
              , pp. 762 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Formal categories
              %strong 17
              (1965) 758-801 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.4153/CJM-1965-076-0"}> doi:10.4153/CJM-1965-076-0
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.cambridge.org/core/services/aop-cambridge-core/content/view/A7C463460EB8CAC64C2CA340F870CF80/S0008414X00039729a.pdf/formal-categories.pdf"} pdf
          %p Though see also the following, which uses more modern terminology:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Max+Kelly"}> Max Kelly
              , §2 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Adjunction for enriched categories
              = succeed "," do
                %em Reports of the Midwest Category Seminar III
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 106
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0059145"} doi:10.1007/BFb0059145
          %p A thorough 2-categorical account is contained in:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Claude Auderset:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Adjonctions et monades au niveau des
                    = succeed "-cat\u00E9gories" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mn 2
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cahiers"} Cahiers
                de topologie et géométrie différentielle
                %strong 15
                1 (1974) 3-20.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Schanuel"}> Stephen Schanuel
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"} Ross Street
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The free adjunction
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cahiers"} Cahiers
                de topologie et géométrie différentielle catégoriques
                %strong 27
                1 (1986) 81-8
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+MacLane"}> Saunders MacLane
                , §XII.4 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+for+the+Working+Mathematician"} Categories for the Working Mathematician
                %strong 5
                Springer (second ed. 1997) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4757-4721-8"}> doi:10.1007/978-1-4757-4721-8
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Lack10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steve+Lack"}> Steve Lack
                , §2.1 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A 2-categories companion
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Towards+Higher+Categories"} Towards Higher Categories
                %strong 152
                Springer (2010) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.CT/0702535"}> arXiv:math.CT/0702535
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4419-1524-5_4"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4419-1524-5_4
            %li#JohnsonYau20
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Niles+Johnson"}> Niles Johnson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Donald+Yau"} Donald Yau
                = succeed "," do
                  %em 2-Dimensional Categories
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/2002.06055"} arXiv:2002.06055
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://oxford.universitypressscholarship.com/view/10.1093/oso/9780198871378.001.0001/oso-9780198871378"} doi:10.1093/oso/9780198871378.001.0001
          %p
            Fr the special case of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
            see any text on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            (and see the references at
            = succeed ")," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint functor
          %ul
            %li#Borceux94
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
                , Vol 1, Section 3 of
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Categorical+Algebra"} Handbook of Categorical Algebra
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes"} geometry of physics – categories and toposes
                  –
                  %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#Adjunctions"} Adjunctions
          %p For some early history and illustrative examples see
          %ul
            %li#Lambek82
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joachim+Lambek"}> Joachim Lambek
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Influence of Heraclitus on Modern Mathematics
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Scientific Philosophy Today: Essays in Honor of Mario Bunge
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-94-009-8462-2_6"} doi:10.1007/978-94-009-8462-2_6
              %p
                (more along these lines at
                = succeed ")." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objective+logic"} objective logic
          %p
            The fundamental role of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
            in
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logic"} logic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            originates with the observation that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/substitution"} substitution
            forms an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/existential+quantification"} existential quantification
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+quantification"} universal quantification
          %ul
            %li#Lawvere69
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"}> William Lawvere
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Adjointness in Foundations
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.emis.de/journals/TAC/reprints/articles/16/tr16abs.html"} tac:16
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"}> William Lawvere
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantifiers and sheaves
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.mathunion.org/ICM/ICM1970.1/Main/icm1970.1.0329.0334.ocr.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Adjunctions in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/programming+languages"} programming languages
            (though mainly again just
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
          %ul
            %li#Hinze12
              %p
                Ralf Hinze,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Generic Programming with Adjunctions
                %em Generic and Indexed Programming
                Lecture Notes in Computer Science, vol 7470. Springer 2012 (
                %a{:href => "http://www.cs.ox.ac.uk/ralf.hinze/LN.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                %a{:href => "http://www.cs.ox.ac.uk/ralf.hinze/SSGIP10/Slides.pdf"} slides
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-32202-0_2"} doi:10.1007/978-3-642-32202-0_2
            %li
              %p
                Jeremy Gibbons, Fritz Henglein, Ralf Hinze, Nicolas Wu,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Relational Algebra by Way of Adjunctions
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.cs.ox.ac.uk/jeremy.gibbons/publications/reladj.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://dl.acm.org/citation.cfm?doid=3243631.3236781"} doi:10.1145/3236781
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adjoint_functors"} Adjoint Functors
            %li
              %p
                Catsters,
                %em Adjunctions
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=loOJxIOmShE&feature=channel_page"}> YouTube
                )
          %hr/
